#!/bin/sh
# fcc-net: what FCC Linux may reach right now (FCC decides, outside Linux).
case "$1" in
  ""|status)
    wget -qO- http://fcc.status/ 2>/dev/null || echo "FCC didn't answer (is this FCC Linux on FCC Phone?)"
    ;;
  *)
    cat <<'HELP'
fcc-net: FCC Linux's internet.

  fcc-net          what's switched on (internet, GitHub token, plugins)

The internet is off until you switch it on in FCC (Lab, FCC Linux). Then:
  - use http:// addresses: FCC makes them https outside Linux, e.g.
      wget -qO- http://api.github.com/zen
  - pip, npm, cargo and go install packages through FCC;
  - fcc-github clones, pulls and pushes GitHub repositories;
  - fcc-plugin calls a plugin you switched on in More, Plugins.
Sites that don't let apps in a browser reach them don't work from the phone.
HELP
    ;;
esac
